<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Tanahun</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1782 CE (approx.) · capital Tanahun</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Sen hill kingdom of central Nepal and one of the Chaubise Rajya, a neighbour and rival of Gorkha and Lamjung.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Tanahun was founded by a branch of the Sen dynasty of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-palpa">Palpa</a> in the early 16th century, after the realm of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mukunda-sen">Mukunda Sen</a> was divided among his heirs. It held hill country along the Marsyangdi and Seti rivers, east of the Kingdom of Palpa and south of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-lamjung">Kingdom of Lamjung</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>As one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaubise-rajya">Chaubise Rajya</a>, the twenty-four principalities of the central hills, Tanahun was ruled by Sen kings who were linked by marriage to other hill dynasties. Little is recorded of its administration. In the 18th century its ruler Trivikram Sen tried to resist <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gorkha-kingdom">Gorkha</a> expansion through alliances with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-lamjung">Lamjung</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-palpa">Palpa</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gorkha-kingdom">Gorkha</a> forces of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-nepal">Kingdom of Nepal</a> annexed Tanahun in 1782 during the unification of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a> under the regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahadur-shah-of-nepal">Bahadur Shah</a>. It is now Tanahun district.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1500 CE – 1782 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.55%;width:5.61%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 CE – 1782 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tanahun</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Trivikram Sen</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Nepali</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/nepal">Nepal</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tanahun, Tanahu</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1641&amp;focus=kingdom-of-tanahun" aria-label="Kingdom of Tanahun on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6875 1149 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Tanahun lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7239 1418h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7195 1405h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7195 1405h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Nepal. <a href="/atlas?year=1641&amp;focus=kingdom-of-tanahun">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

